Z||000000||Formula||05-22-2000||09:51 PM||||1.ok, I want to recarpet my floor, would the sport ute rear carpet stuff they sell in autozone look nice if I glue it to the original carpet? (the $30 kind)<P>2A.I need a new headliner, but I think it would look cool to have black carpet it up there and have grey carpet complement the grey stripe on my car.  Has anyone ever seen a carpeted roof? 2B. Has anyone done this?<P>3.Where can I buy those rubber seat covers that we were talking about on here earlier? I believe they were on horsepower tv too.<P>4.Have any of you had a good experience with seat covers in the $100-$175 range for both seats? If so, what was so good? (I want black or dark grey that wont fade)<P>5A.What kind of paint should I use to paint my interior trim pieces with?  5B. What is the name of the dark grey that came in formulas? 5C. Have you ever painted the interior pieces?<P>6.What have you seen done to a fiero interior that looks cool for a reasonable price?<P>I want to thank you in advance for your cooperation and thoughtful opinions.  Have a nice afternoon!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||05-22-2000||10:09 PM||||Formula, This is all I can come up with,<P>How much $$$ do you want to send? I've never seen the Autozone carpet but do not put in the cheap stuff! $100.00 will get you a GOOD! set of stock seat skins/covers.<P> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451561&Sequence=2" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451561&Sequence=2</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=16992153&Sequence=5" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=16992153&Sequence=5</A> <P><BR>I got my seat skins/covers from a forum member for alot less than $100 and they are in like new condition. Carbon Fiber all done by me.<P>Hope this helps some ?<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||05-23-2000||01:01 AM||||I've done several things to my 86GT and my (former) Dino kit.  You can paint the dash and other plastic parts of the interior with a good interior dash paint.  One word of advice...keep a can handy for touch ups.  My dash never chipped or scratched but the door handles did need an occasional spray.  Both of my cars have black head liners that any upholstery place can do fairly in-expensively, but be carefull taking out the old headliner, it can easily be damaged.  You'll need the foam stuff under the material.<BR>  Seats look real cool when they are done right.  Don't be cheap when it comes to seats.  My advice would be to get covers until you can afford to get them re-upholstered.  Mine ran me $800 Canadian for Ferrari tan leather, double stitched with a custom logo on the headrest.  My black vinyl and cloth seats with logo cost me about  $600 Canadian.  If you do get them re-covered I suggest removing the metal form inside the side of the seat where they always rip.  I had mine removed and stuffed with more padding to hold the form.  4years and no rips on my cloth interior, it looks brand new and they are for sale.  If you're from Toronto and are interested leave post and I'll send you some photos.<BR>It may not be worth shipping because of tax and duty to the U.S.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Jay||05-23-2000||01:03 AM||||Oh yeah, forgot to mention, by next week I'll have photos of my new interior on my web page at <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
